{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The 'arrived' event at 18:15:10 was not an arrival, and the rider's complaint about it is made out on the platform's own trace. No admissible fix places the vehicle inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at or before that timestamp: the first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 18:17:10, a derived dwell_start_offset_sec of -120.0 s, i.e. the app displayed an arrival two minutes before the vehicle entered the geofence. The driver_track's single stationary speed value (0.0 kph) belongs to the 22-fix in-geofence run that only begins at 18:17:10; every other speed value in the trace lies between 32.2 and 46.8 kph, all above POL-NS-05's 15 kph motion threshold. The driver also concedes the point in his own statement on the dispute record ('I pressed arrived a bit early'). Under POL-NS-05 the marker does not start the waiting clock, the clock runs from 18:17:10, and the false-arrival event must be recorded against the driver in the ruling's referrals. I do not claim this alone refunds the fee; the rider's submission on the money is the limb (b) point below.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02725", "EV-TRIP-02725", "EV-CHAT-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account - that the app announced an arrival that had not happened - is corroborated by the driver's own message. At 18:15:30, twenty seconds after the 'I'm Here' tap and 100 seconds before the first admissible in-geofence fix at 18:17:10, the driver wrote 'im at the pickup point'. Read against the trace's own geofence test, that message asserted a presence at the pin that no admissible fix had yet established, and the rider read it at 18:16:00 while the vehicle was still outside the 50 m radius.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02725", "EV-GPS-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (b) is not made out on this record, so the fee is not chargeable. Limb (b)'s first branch requires a fix inside the pickup geofence at or before the 'arrived' event, and the trace contains none before 18:17:10. Its fallback branch opens only where POL-NS-05 finds the marker false, and that finding turns on two numbers - the driver's distance from the pin and his speed at 18:15:10 - neither of which this export supplies: driver_track reports only a minimum, mean and maximum distance across the whole trace, and no derived fact states the vehicle's position or speed at the marker. The party asserting that money is owed carries the burden of proving the facts that make it owed (POL-GEN-07(1)), and a charge is the exception while no charge is the default (POL-GEN-07(2)). The 4.50 carried on EV-FARE-02725 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, cancellation_fee 4.50) is therefore not established on the record as supplied and should be returned to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02725", "EV-TRIP-02725", "EV-FARE-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-GEN-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing external excuses the driver's absence from the geofence in the 120 seconds after he marked arrival. The traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-02725-01 is MISSING for this trip - issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0 - and its absence is itself citable: no KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covered Blk 108 Yishun Ring Rd in this window. With no advisory on the pickup road, holding position at the pin was lawfully possible throughout, and POL-NS-06(i) cannot be used to excuse or accumulate any part of the driver's time outside the radius.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02725-01", "EV-GPS-02725", "EV-TRIP-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Honest concession, so that the arithmetic is not in dispute between us: measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, the driver's continuous run is 210 seconds (22 consecutive qualifying fixes from 18:17:10 to 18:20:40), and the derived shortfall against the free waiting period is -30.0 seconds, i.e. a surplus of 30 seconds. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec as POL-NS-01(c) directs. The rider therefore does not press a POL-NS-06 waiting-period shortfall, and does not put the 300 second figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec in issue, because the resolution rule applies that figure only to records authored before policy version 2 and this record carries platform_policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02725", "EV-TRIP-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, if the judge cannot determine whether the arrival marker was false on this export, the record is one on which two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival and no clause resolves the conflict on the facts supplied: the trip_record's 'arrived' event states 18:15:10 while the gps_trace's first admissible in-geofence fix is 18:17:10, 120 seconds later, and POL-NS-05 can only bridge that gap by a distance and a speed at the marker timestamp that the export does not carry. That engages POL-NS-09(b), and the consequence is a human reviewer rather than an automated collection: the disputed 4.50 is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded. A fee that is held is a fee the rider has not paid, and on a record that cannot settle whether the displayed arrival was real, the charge should not be executed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02725", "EV-GPS-02725"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-05", "POL-GEN-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(iii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09725 for the 'I'm Here' tap on trip TRP-02725 at 2026-08-22T18:15:10 — no qualifying in-geofence fix exists before 18:17:10 (dwell_start_offset_sec -120.0 s) and the vehicle was in motion outside the 50 m pickup radius — so that the pattern is visible to POL-NS-07 and to human review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02725 stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60. The rider is right about the arrival announcement, and that is the one point that goes against the driver. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02725) carries the driver's 'I'm Here' tap at 18:15:10, but the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02725, COMPLETE, weight_multiplier 1.0, 100.0% coverage, 10-second cadence, no gaps, 85 fixes) contains no fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius until 18:17:10 — a derived dwell_start_offset_sec of -120.0 s. The trace's only stationary stretch is the 210-second run from 18:17:10 to 18:20:40; every other fix is recorded at 32.2 to 46.8 km/h, so at 18:15:10 the vehicle was in motion and above POL-NS-05's 15 km/h threshold. The driver also concedes the point in his statement ('I pressed arrived a bit early but I did wait at the pin'). Under POL-NS-05 the marker is FALSE and does not start the waiting clock. What follows. The clock is recomputed under POL-NS-05 to run from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10. On that clock the driver held position at the pin for 210 seconds — 22 consecutive qualifying fixes, each inside the 50 m radius and inside the 25 m accuracy filter — against the free waiting period in force for this trip of 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null), a surplus of 30 seconds (derived shortfall_sec -30.0). The trip was then terminated by the driver at 18:20:41 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, 31 seconds after the required dwell had elapsed. POL-NS-05(iii) therefore applies: the corrected dwell meets the minimum, the false marker does not by itself defeat the fee, and POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full on the recomputed clock. Nothing from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it: POL-NS-06 cannot open because there is no shortfall; POL-NS-03 has no application because the stationary fixes lie inside the 50 m radius, not outside it; POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider because the chat log (EV-CHAT-02725) holds exactly one message and it was sent by the driver at 18:15:30, with no rider message and no in-app call; and POL-NS-10 is not engaged because the driver, not the rider, cancelled. The rider's arguments. The rider submits that POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails because no fix places the vehicle inside the geofence at or before the arrival tap, that limb (b)'s fallback branch needs a distance and a speed at the marker that the export does not carry, and that the burden of proving the charge therefore fails (POL-GEN-07(1)-(2)), so the SGD 4.50 should be returned. That is rejected. Limb (b)'s first branch does fail, but the fallback branch is the one that runs here: POL-NS-05's test is decidable from the record, because the trace shows a single stationary interval beginning only at 18:17:10 with every fix outside it at 32.2 km/h or more, and because the driver admits the early tap; the marker is false and limb (b) is read from the first qualifying in-geofence fix. POL-GEN-07 is not reached: clauses of the policy in force do license an outcome on these facts. The rider's alternative submission that this is an unresolvable arrival contradiction under POL-NS-09(b) is likewise rejected: the arrival tap and the trace are not two admissible artifacts contradicting each other with nothing to resolve them — POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves exactly this gap, and it is why the fee survives. The rider's remaining points are accepted and made no difference to the money: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02725-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT covered the pickup road, POL-NS-06(i) cannot accumulate any time outside the radius, and the driver's 120 seconds outside the geofence are simply not counted; and the rider's concession of the 210-second run with a -30.0-second shortfall is the same arithmetic this ruling uses. The driver's arguments. The four limbs of POL-NS-01 are satisfied, but limb (b) only through POL-NS-05's recomputed clock, not at the arrival tap as the submission implies; the driver's assertion that the trace places him at the pin 'at any point in the waiting window' is right from 18:17:10 onward and wrong for the two minutes before it. POL-NS-02 is satisfied: there are 22 qualifying in-radius fixes, far more than the three consecutive fixes required, and the closest fix is 0.11 m from the pin. POL-NS-04 is closed at limb (a) as the driver says — the only chat message was his own — and the rider_track data (70 fixes, all stationary, 840 to 848 m from the pin, zero qualifying rider-presence fixes) is accepted as context but is not needed to decide the fee. The fare arithmetic is intact: the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd and the fee_schedule default, payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, and the waiting-time line of SGD 0.00 is not claimed, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect and no POL-NS-10(d) issue arises. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 net fee, which the money block returns as SGD 3.60, and the anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4-or-more limb, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 65 is 0.015, below the 0.08 rate limb. The lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_deviation_flags mentioned in that submission are context-only under POL-GEN-01, were flagged as such, and were not used as a ground of decision. No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is present: the counterparty-dispute counters are 0 on both profiles, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, anti-farming does not trip, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other, and every artifact carrying a deciding fact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0. The money. The rider's claim is not supported, so the fee stands as it presently is (NO_ACTION as to the fee), and the outcome the case produces is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60 as POL-GEN-03 requires. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue. Confidence and weight. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact — EV-TRIP-02725, EV-GPS-02725, EV-FARE-02725 and EV-DPROF-02725 — is COMPLETE with weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap on confidence is 1.0. EV-ADVIS-02725-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, carries no fact, and is disclosed by both sides as neutral. Confidence is set at 0.95, above the 0.70 floor in POL-NS-09. Referral. POL-NS-05(iii) directs that the false arrival be recorded against the driver so that the pattern is visible to POL-NS-07 and to human review; that referral is carried in this ruling."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(iii) false-arrival record: driver DRV-09725 tapped 'I'm Here' at 18:15:10 while outside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and travelling above the 15 km/h motion threshold, 120 seconds before the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10. Record the false-arrival event against the driver for human review and for POL-NS-07 pattern monitoring."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "This ruling decides the SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider on 22 August 2026 and not yet refunded (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 on EV-FARE-02725).\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 18:15:10, but no admissible fix places the vehicle inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at that moment: the first qualifying in-geofence fix is at 18:17:10, exactly 120 seconds later (derived dwell_start_offset_sec −120). The only stationary speeds recorded anywhere in the trace belong to the in-geofence run that begins at 18:17:10; the vehicle's other recorded speeds run from 32.2 to 46.8 km/h, all above POL-NS-05's 15 km/h motion threshold. The driver's own statement on the dispute record ('I pressed arrived a bit early') concedes the point, and the rider's complaint that the app announced an arrival that had not happened is made out. Under POL-NS-05 the arrival marker was FALSE and did not start the waiting clock; the clock is recomputed to run from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10.\n\nWhy the fee still stands. On the recomputed clock the driver held position inside the geofence continuously for 210 seconds (22 qualifying fixes, 18:17:10 to 18:20:40) against the free waiting period of 180 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec as POL-NS-01(c) directs; no_show_threshold_sec is null, so nothing longer applies, and the 300-second figure in fee_schedule.minimum_dwell_sec is retained only to interpret pre-version-2 records, which this is not. The derived shortfall is −30 seconds, a 30-second surplus, and the driver terminated the trip at 18:20:41 under RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, one second after the recomputed dwell elapsed. POL-NS-05(iii) applies in terms: where the corrected dwell meets the minimum, the false marker does not by itself defeat the fee and POL-NS-01 governs on the recomputed clock, its limb (b) being expressly read from that first qualifying in-geofence fix. Limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-01 therefore hold on the corrected basis and the SGD 4.50 fee is chargeable.\n\nThe money. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 per cent of the SGD 4.50 net fee, which the money block returns as driver_compensation SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below '4 or more', and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 65 is 0.015, far below 0.08. The ruling value is therefore DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 under POL-GEN-03's single exception; the disposition of the fee itself is NO_ACTION, so the rider's own charge stands as it presently is. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold.\n\nThe rider's submissions. The claim that POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails because the export supplies no position or speed at the marker timestamp is rejected: POL-NS-05 is the clause that reads the marker against the trace, it is satisfied here on the motion trigger and on the driver's own admission, and once the marker is found false limb (b)'s fallback branch opens in terms. The alternative escalation claim under POL-NS-09(b) fails for the same reason: POL-NS-05 resolves the difference between the 18:15:10 event and the 18:17:10 fix, so there is no unresolved contradiction between admissible artifacts on arrival, dwell or rider presence. The rider's own concession on the waiting-period arithmetic (a 30-second surplus, no POL-NS-06 shortfall) is accepted, and the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02725-01 (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not needed for any accumulation, so its absence changes nothing. POL-GEN-07 is not reached: clauses of the policy in force license the outcome, so no residual principle is applied. The rider's submission that the false-arrival event be recorded is granted and appears in the referrals.\n\nThe driver's submissions. The claim that all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold is accepted on the recomputed clock, and the claim that the early tap costs the driver nothing is accepted under POL-NS-05(iii). The reading of POL-NS-01's passage on where the driver's stationary fixes lie - that its 'inside the radius' branch speaks to a termination recorded as DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, not to every driver who reaches the pin - is accepted; read otherwise it would empty limb (c) of content and contradict POL-NS-06 and POL-NS-07, and here the reason code is RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three limb (d) recognises, so no mis-selected-code referral arises. The rider-presence material (rider_track 840 to 848 m from the pin, zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider radius) is not needed to decide, because the fee is decided on the driver's evidence alone.\n\nEvidence, weight and confidence. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 (EV-GPS-02725, EV-TRIP-02725, EV-FARE-02725), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no artifact caps the ruling below the 0.70 floor. No POL-NS-08 limb (a) to (d) is engaged: no clock skew above 90 seconds, no sampling gap above 120 seconds with 85 fixes at a 10-second cadence and full coverage, the chat log holds the single message trip_record records, and the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line reconciles to platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no fare defect. Under POL-GEN-01, driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags and driver_profile.prior_deviation_flags appear in the driver's submission only to state that they are not the fields POL-NS-07 reads; they are context-only, no finding rests on them, and nothing was built on reputation."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(iii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09725. The 'I'm Here' marker was tapped at 18:15:10, 120 seconds before the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10, so the trip record's arrival event did not start the waiting clock. The fee is unaffected; the record is for the driver's file and for human review of the pattern."
    ],
    "confidence": 1.0,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The 4.50 SGD no-show fee charged on trip TRP-02725 stands, and driver DRV-09725 is paid 3.60 SGD compensation, with a false-arrival referral placed on his file.\n\nThe rider's complaint is upheld in part. The 'I'm Here' tap at 18:15:10 was premature: the driver concedes it in his statement ('I pressed arrived a bit early'), and his own trace agrees - no admissible fix places the vehicle inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius before 18:17:10, 120 seconds later (dwell_start_offset_sec -120.0), and the trace's recorded speeds outside the 22-fix stationary run all lie between 32.2 and 46.8 km/h, above the 15 km/h at which POL-NS-05 treats an arrival marker as false. So the app did announce an arrival that had not happened, and that false-arrival event is recorded in the referrals against the driver.\n\nBut POL-NS-05 does not void the fee. It recomputes the waiting clock to run from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and on that corrected clock the driver held position at the pin for 210 continuous seconds (22 qualifying fixes, 18:17:10 to 18:20:40) against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip record platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no longer no_show_threshold_sec is set). He terminated at 18:20:41 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one second after that dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. POL-NS-01 is therefore satisfied in full on the recomputed clock, and POL-NS-05(iii) provides in terms that an early marker which is nonetheless followed by the required dwell does not defeat the fee.\n\nRider Advocate's remaining points. Limb (b) is not failed: its fallback branch opens exactly where the marker is found false, and falsity here is asserted by both parties and admitted by the driver against his own interest, so the finding does not depend on a per-fix distance or speed the export omits; POL-GEN-07(1)-(2) is not reached because clauses of the policy in force do license the outcome. The waiting-period shortfall route (POL-NS-06) fails on the arithmetic both sides agree: 210 s against a 180 s minimum is a 30-second surplus, not a shortfall, so the refund limb cannot open. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02725-01 (MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) establishes only that no kerb restriction, enforcement, closure or accident covered the pickup road, so POL-NS-06(i) could not have been engaged had accumulation been needed - and it was not needed, because the dwell is one continuous qualifying run. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: the only chat message is the driver's ('im at the pickup point', 18:15:30), and the rider's own track carries 70 motionless fixes 840 to 848 m from the pin with none inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, so limb (a) fails and limb (c) is affirmatively failed. The alternative escalation argument fails too: POL-NS-09(b) requires a conflict no clause resolves, and POL-NS-05 resolves this one; the counterparty-dispute counters are 0 on both profiles, rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 termination against 65 completed trips in 30 days is 0.015, below the 0.08 rate limb, and 1 is below the 4-count limb), so no trigger (a) to (e) fires.\n\nDriver's payout. POL-NS-07 pays 80 percent of the 4.50 SGD net cancellation fee read from platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, which the fare-breakdown cancellation-fee line also shows (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), so no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises; the money block returns driver_compensation 3.60 SGD. The lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and play no part in this check.\n\nOn a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling, amount_sgd carries the same 3.60 SGD the ruling moves; the rider's 4.50 SGD charge is left as it presently is and no refund is issued to him. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact - trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown - is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is 1.0; the only impaired artifact, the missing advisory at weight 0.0, carries no deciding fact. The monetary effect of 3.60 SGD is below the 8.00 SGD automatic-execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(iii): record a false-arrival event against driver DRV-09725 on trip TRP-02725 — the 'I'm Here' marker was tapped at 18:15:10, 120 s before the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10 (dwell_start_offset_sec -120.0 s on EV-GPS-02725), so the pattern is visible to POL-NS-07 and to human review; the corrected 210 s dwell met the 180 s minimum, so the fee itself stands."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the record decides this case, and each of you is partly right about what it shows.\n\nWhat happened. The rider is right that the app announced an arrival that had not yet happened. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02725) carries the driver's 'I'm Here' tap at 18:15:10, but his GPS trace (EV-GPS-02725) holds no qualifying fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius until 18:17:10; the derived dwell_start_offset_sec of -120.0 s is exactly that two-minute gap, and every speed recorded in the track is either the 0.0 kph of the in-geofence stationary run or 32.2-46.8 kph, above POL-NS-05's 15 kph motion threshold. The driver concedes it in his own statement: 'I pressed arrived a bit early but I did wait at the pin.' I therefore find the arrival marker FALSE under POL-NS-05, and it did not start the waiting clock. The rider's POL-NS-05 claim is accepted on that point, as is his observation that the driver's 18:15:30 chat message ('im at the pickup point') asserted a presence the trace had not yet established - a message records what a party said, not where he was, and it adds nothing to the marker finding either way.\n\nWhy the fee still stands. POL-NS-05 recomputes the clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 18:17:10, and on that clock the driver held position inside the radius continuously for 210 seconds (22 consecutive qualifying fixes, 18:17:10 to 18:20:40) against the 180 second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null, so nothing longer applies). The derived shortfall is -30.0 s, i.e. a surplus of 30 seconds. POL-NS-05(iii) is explicit: where the corrected dwell nonetheless meets the minimum, the early marker does not by itself defeat the fee and POL-NS-01 governs on the recomputed clock. Limb (b) is satisfied through its second branch (the recomputed first in-geofence fix), limb (a) by the recorded arrival event, limb (c) by the 210 second dwell, and limb (d) because the driver terminated the trip at 18:20:41 - at or after the moment the required period elapsed, with no boarding event, and under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes that limb recognises (not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE). The rider's arguments are answered: that limb (b) fails for want of a fix at or before the marker is met by limb (b)'s own second branch; that POL-GEN-07(1)-(2) puts the charging burden on the driver fails because the clause tests have been run, not left untested; and the alternative request for escalation under POL-NS-09(b) fails because the apparent conflict between the arrival event and the first in-geofence fix is resolved by POL-NS-05 itself, so the 'and no clause resolves the conflict' condition is absent. POL-NS-06 provides no route either, and the rider does not press one: with a single continuous in-geofence run of 210 seconds there is no shortfall to refund.\n\nThe rider's own track is not decisive but is recorded: EV-GPS-02725's rider_track holds 70 stationary fixes 840-848 m from the pickup pin, none inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider (its limb (a) also fails - the only chat message was the driver's). POL-NS-01 does not require the rider to be at the pin, so this does not decide the fee.\n\nThe money. The disputed SGD 4.50 cancellation fee (EV-FARE-02725, cancellation_fee 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is the platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd figure for this trip and reconciles with the fare_breakdown line, so no POL-NS-08(d) defect arises and no waiting-time fee is claimed (POL-NS-10(d) is not in play). The disposition of the fee is NO_ACTION in the sense POL-NS-07 uses - the rider's monetary claim is not supported and the charge stands - while the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, because the fee is payable to the driver. POL-NS-07 fixes his payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 net fee = SGD 3.60, which is the money block's driver_compensation figure; per POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd carries that same SGD 3.60, being the amount the ruling moves. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/65 completed trips is 0.015 (below 0.08), so the case does not escalate under POL-NS-09. No part of this ruling rests on a context-only profile field: the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_deviation_flags appear in one citation and were correctly disclaimed there - under POL-GEN-01 they are reputation context only and cannot carry a finding.\n\nWeights. Every artifact the ruling rests on is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-02725, EV-GPS-02725, EV-FARE-02725, EV-DPROF-02725), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02725-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is not relied on and carries no fact: with one continuous in-geofence run there is nothing for POL-NS-06(i) to accumulate, and the 180 second minimum is met without it. The driver's statement sits on the dispute record and, having no weight multiplier, enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the cap; it corroborates the marker finding the trace already carries.\n\nReferral and execution. POL-NS-05(iii) requires the false-arrival event to be recorded against the driver even though the fee stands, and that referral is issued with this ruling. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes automatically on issue. This is a provisional ruling; either party may appeal once under POL-GEN-04."
